title: Choosing
card: Chapter 3 | Choosing | If, otherwise, and depending on
say: A program often has to choose what to do. That's what if is for.
uncard

new: weather.fathom
type:
  genesis:
    set temperature to 31
    if temperature exceeds 30:
      scrawl "It's hot."
    otherwise if temperature falls below 10:
      scrawl "It's cold."
    otherwise:
      scrawl "It's nice."
  and the universe said i love you
zoom: lines 2-8
spot: lines 3-4
say:
  If temperature exceeds thirty, with a colon. The lines moved in below it happen only when that's yes.
  Exceeds means more than. Falls below means less than. There's also is at least, is at most, is, and is not.
spot: lines 5-6
say: Otherwise if is tried next, only when the ones above it were no.
spot: lines 7-8
say: And otherwise catches everything else.
spot: off
run
zoom: output
say: Thirty one is more than thirty, so it's hot.
wait
zoom: out

say: When a choice is about one value, depending on reads better.
clear
type:
  genesis:
    set weather to "snow"
    depending on weather:
      "rain": scrawl "Take an umbrella."
      "snow", "hail":
        scrawl "Wear a coat."
        scrawl "And boots."
      anything else: scrawl "Enjoy the day."
  and the universe said i love you
zoom: lines 2-8
spot: line 3
say: Depending on weather looks at the weather once.
spot: line 4
say: Each line under it is a value, a colon, and what to do. A short choice fits on the same line.
spot: lines 5-7
say: Several values can share one choice, with commas between them, and a longer choice goes on its own lines below.
spot: line 8
say: Anything else is for every other value.
spot: off
run
zoom: output
say: It's snowing, so: wear a coat, and boots.
wait
zoom: out

say: Choices can be joined together with and, or, and not, and is one of checks a value against several at once.
clear
type:
  genesis:
    set answer to "y"
    set hungry to yes
    if answer is one of ("yes", "y", "sure") and not hungry:
      scrawl "Let's go now."
    otherwise if hungry or answer is "later":
      scrawl "Lunch first."
  and the universe said i love you
zoom: lines 2-7
spot: line 4
say: Answer is one of yes, y, or sure. And not hungry.
spot: line 6
say: Hungry or answer is later.
spot: off
run
zoom: output
say: We are hungry, so: lunch first.
wait
zoom: out

card: Chapter 3 | Testing | Checks that say what should be so
say:
  How do you know a program is right? You test it. A check line says something that should be so.
uncard
clear
type:
  to double, given x (a number), returning a number:
    return x times 2
  and the universe said i love you

  to test doubling:
    check double with 2 is 4
    check double with 0 is 0
    check double with -3 is -6
  and the universe said i love you

  genesis:
    scrawl double with 21
  and the universe said i love you
zoom: lines 1-3
say:
  This is a command of our own, called double. We'll see commands properly soon. For now: it takes a number, and gives back twice that number.
zoom: lines 5-9
say:
  A command whose name starts with test holds checks. Check double with two is four.
  Checks don't run when the program runs. They run when you press Test.
zoom: out
test
zoom: output
say: Every check passed.
wait
zoom: out
say: Now let's make one fail on purpose, to see what that looks like.
line: 7
keys: backspace
type: 1
test: expect a failure
zoom: output
say: The test failed, and Fathom says which line, and the check that wasn't so.
wait
zoom: out

card: Chapter 3 | Watching | Seeing a program think
say: Last, the Watch button. It runs a program one line at a time, and shows what each line did.
uncard
clear
type:
  genesis:
    set temperature to 31
    if temperature exceeds 30:
      scrawl "It's hot."
    otherwise:
      scrawl "It's nice."
  and the universe said i love you
watch
zoom: output
say:
  Each line is shown as it happens. Line two set temperature to thirty one.
  Line three asked if it exceeds thirty, and the answer was yes. So line four said: it's hot.
  When a program does something you don't expect, watching it is the quickest way to find out why.
wait
zoom: out
